# Catalogue content

Author definitions as JSON documents (one file per entity):

- Response / Modify → `src/server/content/cards/<card-id>.json`
- Fighters (engine type creature) → `src/server/content/creatures/<creature-id>.json`
- Named faces → `src/server/content/faces/<face-id>.json`
- One shared deck per team → `src/server/content/loadouts/<id>.json`

JSON must satisfy `src/server/content/schema/*.schema.json`. Inspect the
schema before adding a field. Content model:
`.cursor/skills/author-content/design.md` and
`docs/specs/030-offensive-control.md`.

Id constants stay in `cards.ts` / `creatures.ts` / `faces.ts`.
Effects are AST `op` nodes or legacy `type` members compiled by `AstCompiler`.

Rules:

- `type` is `response` or `modify`. Block, Dodge, Counter, prevent, and
  redirect are effects. `modifySubject` is `roll`, `die`, `moveset`,
  `target`, or `tag`. Do not author Instant, Reaction, Equipment, Overload,
  or Ritual as the card kind. Leftover regions with those names are not a
  pattern.
- Faces are named inputs (name, type, primary, secondary). No generic Guard,
  Block, Dodge, or Counter face. The `face-natural|synthetic|untyped-` id
  prefix is a validator token, not a kind. No Shield resource. No
  deckbuilding dice. `baseDie` on the Fighter is the die a match starts from.
- `fighterRestriction` is a play check, not a deck ban. One deck and one hand
  per player. Tag is an operation. Assist is Fighter-owned.
- Lifecycle is `one-shot` or `persistent`. Meter is exceptional
  (`exceptionalMeterCost`), not mana on every strong card.
- `rulesText` uses [`docs/KEYWORDS.md`](docs/KEYWORDS.md). Prefer
  `[Mark N X]` / `[Strip N X]` / `[Modify]`. Do not copy pile-era
  `[Forge 1 Synthetic …]` or attribute exclusives onto new print.
- Structured fields only when every clause is modelled. Gaps go to
  `docs/DEFERRED_CATALOGUE.md`.
- Schemas may still require `forge` or `attacks`. Satisfy them. Do not
  design pile `[Spend]` / `[Requires]` or a legendary win around those fields.
- Print voice is the holder: `you` / `opponent`.
- Follow `.cursor/skills/author-content/SKILL.md`.
- Live JSON is catalogue truth. `docs/MECHANIC_ARCHETYPES.md` pile-era rows
  are not a pattern.
